{"causes": ["The election of his maternal uncle, Giuliano della Rovere, as Pope Julius II in 1503 provided the primary catalyst for his rapid ecclesiastical advancement.", "The established tradition of nepotism within the Renaissance Papacy allowed powerful families to consolidate influence and wealth through the appointment of relatives to high office.", "The strategic need for Pope Julius II to secure loyal administrators and allies within the College of Cardinals and the Papal States facilitated Sisto's promotion."], "effects": ["Sisto Gara della Rovere's cardinalate solidified the della Rovere family's political and ecclesiastical power base within the Roman Curia and the Papal States.", "His administrative roles in various bishoprics contributed to the governance and financial management of papal territories during a period of significant political upheaval.", "His presence in the College of Cardinals reinforced papal authority and provided a reliable vote for the policies and interests of Pope Julius II and later Pope Leo X."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "julius-ii", "sourceName": "Pope Julius II", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "sisto-gara-della-rovere", "targetName": "Sisto Gara della Rovere", "context": "Pope Julius II, Sisto's maternal uncle, profoundly influenced his career by elevating him to cardinal in 1507 and granting him multiple bishoprics."}, {"sourceSlug": "sisto-gara-della-rovere", "sourceName": "Sisto Gara della Rovere", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "fifth-lateran-council", "targetName": "Fifth Lateran Council", "context": "Sisto Gara della Rovere participated in the Fifth Lateran Council, an ecumenical council of the Catholic Church from 1512 to 1517."}, {"sourceSlug": "sisto-gara-della-rovere", "sourceName": "Sisto Gara della Rovere", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "rome-papal-states", "targetName": "Rome, Papal States", "context": "Sisto Gara della Rovere's primary ecclesiastical and political activities, including